            "review_title": "Review at Emoji Pizza",
            "review_text": "Joseph Cao\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4 contributions\n0\nCozy place and Fine Wood Fired Pizza\nJul 2019 • Family\nUse your google map to locate the restaurant or you might miss it (it's kinda hidden). The place is cozy and quiet. There isn't much room between tables though so watch your kids if they are too active. The pizzas are fine. The base is soft (not too soft) and thin so you won't get full quickly (I like this). The bacons, sausages taste and smell good. Compared to other pizza 'franchises' you will have better meal with around the same price. The only down side is you don't get to choose the size of your pizza. Only 9' for each type of pizza. There are also side dishes but I didn't try any. The services and staffs are too nice. There's one customer that tripped and slam on my brother. There wasn't any thing serious but the staff apologized later and gave us free desserts. That was unexpected nice. I never gave 5 stars before but this one deserves it.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten July 19, 2019",
